# Plan: customer satisfaction rating

Spec: `docs/specs/csat-rating.md` (approved, Mai Do, 2026-01-12). Written 2026-10-07. Nothing is built.
Test command: `node --test` (README; `npm` is not installed on this host, so run `node --test` directly).

## Goal

Customers rate a resolved ticket 1-5 from the portal, once. A 1 or 2 emails the owner. A nightly job writes
a per-agent weekly summary. `assignee_id` becomes `owner_id`.

## Phases

| # | Phase | Covers | Class | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | [Rename `assignee_id` to `owner_id`](phase-01-rename-owner.md) | R6 | COUNCIL (external export contract, schema) | todo |
| 2 | [Rate a resolved ticket](phase-02-rate-ticket.md) | R1, R2, R3 | ACT (the Postgres change is outside the repo) | todo |
| 3 | [Email the owner on a 1 or 2](phase-03-low-score-email.md) | R4 | ACT | todo |
| 4 | [Weekly summary job, docs, review](phase-04-weekly-summary.md) | R5 | ACT, then independent review | todo |

Rename goes first so every later line is written as `owner_id` and is not edited twice.

## Dependencies

- Phase 2 needs 1. Phase 3 needs 2. Phase 4 needs 2 (and reads the owner from 1).
- Outside this repo, and not done by this plan: the Postgres migration (phase 1 step 7, phase 2 step 7), finance's
  reporting job, the nightly scheduler entry for the new job. Each is a handoff item.

## Decisions (answers recommended in the user's absence; work proceeds from them)

| Q | Question | Recommended answer, used by this plan |
|---|---|---|
| Q1 | The finance job reads `exports/tickets.json` and deploys on its own schedule. Rename the exported field outright? | No. The export writes `owner_id` and also `assignee_id` with the same value, marked TEMPORARY, expiring 2026-11-30. Finance moves to `owner_id`, then the alias is deleted in its own change. A hard rename would break their job silently. |
| Q2 | Does the rename include the function `assignTicket` and the glossary word "Assignee"? | Field only, as the spec says. `assignTicket` stays (it is the verb). The glossary entry becomes "Owner", with "formerly assignee" so old notes still resolve. |
| Q3 | Which tickets can be rated? | Only `resolved`, as the spec's criteria say. A resolved ticket closes after 3 days without an answer (`src/jobs/close-resolved.js:5`), so the window is about 3 days. Mai should know. A customer answer reopens the ticket; a rating already given stays and cannot be given again. |
| Q4 | Where is the rating stored? | On the ticket row: `rating`, `rated_at` (spec: "stored with the ticket"). It survives the purge job, which only deletes messages. |
| Q5 | Two customers rate the same ticket at the same moment. | `store.rateTicket` is a conditional set that returns false if a rating exists. The Postgres adapter must do `UPDATE ... WHERE id=$1 AND rating IS NULL` and report whether a row changed. |
| Q6 | Whose weekly figures does a rating count toward when the ticket was reassigned after rating? | The current `owner_id`. Simple, matches "their tickets". Snapshotting the agent at rating time is more code for a rare case. |
| Q7 | Where does the weekly summary go, and in what shape? | `exports/csat-weekly.json`, next to the ticket export, rewritten each night: `[{agent_id, ratings, average}]`, rolling past seven days, average to 2 decimals, agents with no ratings left out. The spec does not say where; this is the least new surface. |
| Q8 | A 1 or 2 on a ticket nobody owns? | No email and no error (`notifyAgent` throws without an agent, `src/notify.js:7`). The rating is still stored. |

## Execution

Inline in one session with a checkpoint after each phase, or a subagent per phase. Recommended: inline, phase 1
reviewed before phase 2 starts. Commit per task (conventional commits).

## Self-review against the spec

R1 phase 2 steps 1-4. R2 phase 2 test "a second rating is refused". R3 phase 2 test "another organisation". R4
phase 3. R5 phase 4. R6 phase 1. Every acceptance criterion has a named test in the phase that builds it. Names used
across phases: `owner_id`, `rating`, `rated_at`, `store.rateTicket`, `portal.rateTicket`, `weeklyCsat`.
